Prerequisites
## Prerequisites

Install the following before starting:

- Python 3.11 recommended
- Docker Desktop
- Minikube
- kubectl
- Helm
- Ollama

Install Minikube
## Step 1 — Start Kubernetes Cluster

```bash
minikube start
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Enable Metrics Server
## Step 2 — Enable Metrics Server

```bash
minikube addons enable metrics-server
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl top pods
```
Install Helm
## Step 3 — Install Helm

Verify:

```bash
helm version
```
Install Prometheus + Grafana
## Step 4 — Install Prometheus & Grafana

Add repository:

```bash
helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
```

```bash
helm repo update
```

Install stack:

```bash
helm install monitoring prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack
```
Access Grafana
## Step 5 — Access Grafana

Port forward:

```bash
kubectl port-forward svc/monitoring-grafana 3000:80
```

Open:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

Get password:

```bash
kubectl get secret monitoring-grafana -o jsonpath="{.data.admin-password}" | base64 --decode
```
Install Loki
## Step 6 — Install Loki

Add repo:

```bash
helm repo add grafana https://grafana.github.io/helm-charts
```

```bash
helm repo update
```

Install Loki:

```bash
helm install loki grafana/loki-stack
```
Install Ollama
## Step 7 — Install Ollama

Install Ollama application.

Pull model:

```bash
ollama pull phi3:mini
```

Verify:

```bash
ollama list
```
Install Python Dependencies
## Step 8 — Install Python Dependencies

Create virtual environment:

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate:

### Git Bash

```bash
source venv/Scripts/activate
```

### PowerShell

```powershell
venv\\Scripts\\activate
```

Install packages:

```bash
pip install chromadb sentence-transformers langchain ollama requests kubernetes
```
Start Services
## Step 9 — Start Required Services

Start Ollama:

```bash
ollama serve
```

Start Grafana:

```bash
kubectl port-forward svc/monitoring-grafana 3000:80
```

Start Prometheus:

```
Run AI Monitor
## Step 10 — Run AI Monitor

```bash
python monitor.py
```

Expected:

```text
Starting AI AIOps Monitor...
```


Testing & Verification
## Step 11 — Verification Tests

### Test CrashLoopBackOff

```bash
kubectl set image deployment my-app my-app=nginx:wrongtag
```

Expected:
- incident generated
- AI analysis created
- email alert received
- remediation triggered

---

### Test Pod Restart

```bash
kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- sh -c "kill 1"
```

Expected:
- restart detected
- incident stored
- AI RCA generated

---

### Test RAG Memory

Trigger same issue twice.

Expected:
- AI references previous incidents
```
